System.Drawing.Common
---------------------

This product includes software from .NET (https://github.com/dotnet/runtime, branch release/6.0, commit 76b9680):
System.Drawing.Common 6.0 (src/libraries/System.Drawing.Common/src and the two Common/src interop files it uses),
licensed under the MIT License:

    Licensed to the .NET Foundation under one or more agreements.
    The .NET Foundation licenses this file to you under the MIT license.

It is in the external/runtime submodule (https://github.com/xforcore/runtime, branch drawingforcore), compiled by
src/drawingForCore.System.Drawing.Common; each file keeps its original header, and every change is a commit on that
branch. The GDI+ engine in SkiaGdiPlus/ is drawingForCore's own, under the MIT License. The assembly carries
System.Drawing.Common's public key (token cc7b13ffcd2ddd51, keys/System.Drawing.Common.snk) so that references to it
resolve; it is public signed, not signed by Microsoft. It uses SkiaSharp (https://github.com/mono/SkiaSharp, MIT
License, Copyright (c) 2015-2016 Xamarin, Inc., Copyright (c) 2017-2018 Microsoft Corporation) and the Skia native
library it ships (BSD 3-Clause, Copyright (c) 2011 Google Inc.).

System.Drawing
--------------

src/drawingForCore.System.Drawing comes from WebFormsForCore (https://github.com/webformsforcore/WebFormsForCore,
commit 52f4172, src/WebFormsForCore.Drawing/AssemblyInfo.cs), MIT License, Copyright (c) 2024 Simon Jakob Egli: the
assembly's attributes and its type forwards to System.Drawing.Common. It was copied once
and is kept in this repository. The assembly carries
System.Drawing's public key (token b03f5f7f11d50a3a, keys/System.Drawing.snk); it is public signed, not signed by
Microsoft.

Tests
-----

System.Drawing.Common 6.0's tests (src/libraries/System.Drawing.Common/tests, the Common/tests files they link, and
src/libraries/Common/tests/TestUtilities with the Common/src interop files it links), from the same dotnet/runtime
commit and under the same licence, live in test/drawingForCore.System.Drawing.Common.Tests and
test/drawingForCore.TestUtilities. They run on Microsoft.DotNet.XUnitExtensions and Microsoft.DotNet.RemoteExecutor
from the .NET Arcade SDK (https://github.com/dotnet/arcade, branch release/6.0, commit 565a800,
src/Microsoft.DotNet.XUnitExtensions/src and src/Microsoft.DotNet.RemoteExecutor/src;
test/drawingForCore.Microsoft.DotNet.XUnitExtensions and test/drawingForCore.Microsoft.DotNet.RemoteExecutor), and use
test data from .NET Runtime Assets (https://github.com/dotnet/runtime-assets, branch release/6.0, commit 848e27e:
System.Drawing.Common.TestData, System.ComponentModel.TypeConverter.TestData, System.Windows.Extensions.TestData; in
the tests' TestData folder). Both are licensed under the MIT License, Copyright (c) .NET Foundation and Contributors.
They are in the external/runtime, external/arcade and external/runtime-assets submodules
(https://github.com/xforcore/runtime, arcade and runtime-assets, branch drawingforcore); every change is a commit on
those branches.

The test data's fonts (Code New Roman, (c) 2015 TypoStyle Co.) are not committed: the font's own licence text both
grants the SIL Open Font License 1.1 and forbids redistribution. tools/ci/fetch-test-fonts.sh downloads them from
dotnet/runtime-assets for test runs, and xforcore/runtime-assets' branch removes them. They are never in the
packages.
